      probEyebrow: "Why cloud",
      probTitle: "What problem does it solve?",
      probP1: "Adding check-in to a warehouse usually starts as an IT project. Someone specs a server for the gatehouse, someone else runs cabling to the barrier, a terminal gets mounted and then freezes two months later, and at the second site the whole rollout starts again. Until then, the gate still runs on a paper register and a phone call to the dispatcher.",
      probP2: "Logistiq runs check-in entirely in the cloud. You sign up at logistiq.cloud, name the warehouse, and the platform derives its address itself: \"Depozit Bucuresti\" becomes qrgo.ro/depozit-bucuresti-a3f9k2, live the moment it is created, with no provisioning step. Drivers open that link in any browser, with no account. Operators work in another browser. A second warehouse is one more record and one more link, not one more server.",
