      b2a: "Work from logistiq.cloud in a browser — no terminal to mount, patch or repair.",
      b2c: "No terminal to die at the gate — check-in runs from any browser at hand.",
      b3t: "IT and management",
      b3a: "No servers to provision, patch or back up for the platform itself — Vercel and Supabase host both apps.",
      b3b: "Adding a warehouse claims a plan slot; it never requires new equipment or cabling.",
      b3c: "Physical barrier control is the one add-on that needs equipment: a QRGoBox device on site, off until you switch the gates system on.",
      faqTitle: "Frequently asked questions about the cloud platform",
      q1: "Is there really nothing to install at the warehouse?",
      a1: "For check-in, bookings, the yard map and the dashboard, nothing at all. Operators use a browser at logistiq.cloud, drivers use qrgo.ro/{slug} on their phone. The one exception is physical barrier control: opening a real gate needs a QRGoBox device. That is an optional add-on, switched off until you turn the gates system on.",
      q2: "Can we host Logistiq on our own server?",
      a2: "No. Logistiq is delivered only as a cloud service — there is no installer, no on-premise package and no self-hosted edition. Both apps run on Vercel, and the Supabase backend that holds your data sits in the EU (eu-central-1). If your internal policy requires the software to sit inside your own datacentre, Logistiq is not the right fit.",
      q3: "Do drivers have to install an app?",
      a3: "No. The check-in page at qrgo.ro/{slug} is public and requires no login — the driver opens the link on any phone and fills in the form in one of 12 languages. QRGO Driver is available on the App Store and Google Play for drivers who prefer an app, but it is never required.",
      q4: "What changes when we add a second or a tenth warehouse?",
      a4: "Nothing physical. Each warehouse is a new record with its own automatically generated link, and your plan defines how many slots you have — one on Warehouse Manager, up to 25 on the largest Enterprise plan. If you want drivers to reach a warehouse on your own domain instead of qrgo.ro, that is optional and needs a DNS record on your side.",
