      faqTitle: "Frequently asked questions about automatic location detection",
      q1: "Does the app check the driver in automatically?",
      a1: "No, and that is deliberate. Detection only suggests. When the driver's phone is inside your polygon, the app shows the \"Location Detected\" banner with a Check-in button. Tapping it opens the normal check-in form, where the driver fills in the plate, references and documents as always. Nothing is ever submitted on the strength of a GPS reading alone.",
      q2: "Does it work with the app closed, in the background?",
      a2: "No. The check runs once, when the driver opens the app: a single GPS reading, compared with your zone on the phone itself. There is no background location and no continuous tracking — which also means no battery drain and no permanent permission to explain to drivers. In practice, drivers open the app when they arrive anyway.",
      q3: "Does it work on qrgo.ro, the page opened from the QR code?",
      a3: "No. Location detection lives only in the QRGO Driver app, for iOS and Android. The web check-in page on qrgo.ro stays exactly as it is — QR code or link, no location involved. The web page does offer an \"Open in Maps\" button for navigation to the assigned ramp once a check-in is accepted.",
      q4: "Do we see where drivers are, or when they arrive?",
      a4: "No. The driver's coordinates never leave the phone: the app downloads the zone polygons and does the comparison locally, and no latitude or longitude is stored on a check-in. The arrival notification goes to the driver's own device, not to your team. You see a check-in when the driver submits one, as always.",
