      probTitle: "What problem does it solve?",
      probP1: "It is 07:40 and a driver is standing at the office window. His phone is an old handset with no camera worth the name, or the battery died somewhere on the road. He cannot scan the QR code, so an operator stops what she is doing, asks for the papers and types the check-in herself. Behind him, three more drivers wait, and at the ramp nobody knows yet who arrived.",
      probP2: "QRGO Self puts a tablet and a printer on that counter. The driver fills in the same check-in form the app uses, enters his phone number and confirms it with a code sent by SMS. The check-in lands in the same list your dispatchers already watch, he leaves with a printed ticket, and every instruction after that — ramp 12, please wait — arrives by SMS.",
