      b3b: "Sees the loading / unloading / both split at a glance",
      b3c: "Knows exactly how full the yard is right now",
      faqTitle: "Frequently asked questions about analytics",
      q1: "Which metrics does Logistiq measure?",
      a1: "Wait time (check-in to ramp assigned), processing time (assigned to completed), throughput (check-ins over time), the loading/unloading/both split, and dock & parking utilisation — all derived from the real timestamps on every check-in.",
      q2: "Is the data real-time?",
      a2: "Yes. The counters and charts are computed live over your check-ins via Supabase Realtime, so the numbers move as trucks are checked in, assigned and completed — no manual refresh.",
      q3: "Can I look at different time periods?",
      a3: "Yes. Every metric can be viewed for today, yesterday, the last 7 days, this week, the last 30 days or this month, so you can compare a busy day to a quiet one or track the trend across the month.",
      q4: "Can I break the numbers down by department or operation?",
      a4: "Yes. Utilisation and volume are shown per department and per operation type (loading, unloading, both), and the yard KPI view breaks occupancy down by warehouse, department and parking.",
